WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.790
I hit Buy. Why isn't it filling?

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:12.975
A market order tries to fill quickly at the prices available now,

00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:14.637
but the final price can move.

00:00:14.637 --> 00:00:18.705
A limit order says 'buy no higher' or 'sell no lower' than a set price.

00:00:18.705 --> 00:00:20.310
It isn't guaranteed to fill.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.870
If you want to buy below the current price, you may have to wait. On the other hand,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.050
a limit order that already meets the other side's price can fill right away.

00:00:41.050 --> 00:00:43.360
Not every limit order has to wait in line.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.520
So does cancelling undo what I already bought?

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:07.707
No. Cancel only affects the part that hasn't filled. What already filled stays.

00:01:07.707 --> 00:01:08.820
It doesn't rewind.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.853
Read the status before you act.

00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:29.937
Whether you're the maker or the taker depends on how the trade actually filled.

00:01:29.937 --> 00:01:33.090
Choosing 'limit' doesn't automatically get you a certain fee.

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:43.820
No.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:48.200
Choosing an order type is choosing how it executes. It's not making a wish.

00:01:56.250 --> 00:02:00.530
A green candle. Does it mean the next one goes up too? Next episode.

00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:03.110
Understand first, then act.
